<title>CANADA: TENNIS-CANADIAN OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-CANADIAN OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the $2.3 million</p>
<p>Canadian Open men's tennis tournament on Thursday (prefix</p>
<p>number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Third round</p>
<p>1-Michael Chang (U.S.) beat 15-Alex O'Brien (U.S.) 4-6 6-2</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>Chris Woodruff (U.S.) beat 2-Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia) 7-6</p>
<p>(8-6) 6-2</p>
<p>Fabrice Santoro (France) beat 3-Thomas Muster (Austria) 6-2</p>
<p>2-6 6-4</p>
<p>4-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) beat 13-Wayne Ferreira (South</p>
<p>Africa) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>5-Thomas Enqvist (Sweden) beat 12-Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) 6-3</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>6-Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) beat Michael Tebbutt (Australia)</p>
<p>5-7 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>7-Mark Philippoussis (Australia) beat Guillaume Raoux</p>
<p>(France) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>8-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) beat Justin Gimelstob (U.S.)</p>
<p>6-2 6-4</p>
</text>
